We need to implement an efficient, non-recursive search algorithm in Dafny.  
A good choice is **binary search** on a sorted sequence, as it is efficient (O(log n)) and avoids recursion by using a loop.

Below is the Dafny code that meets the requirements:

```dafny
method BinarySearch(a: seq<int>, key: int) returns (index: int)
    requires forall i, j :: 0 <= i < j < |a| ==> a[i] <= a[j]  // a is sorted in non-decreasing order
    ensures 0 <= index < |a| ==> a[index] == key
    ensures index == -1 ==> forall k :: 0 <= k < |a| ==> a[k] != key
{
    var low := 0;
    var high := |a| - 1;
    index := -1;

    while low <= high
        invariant 0 <= low <= high + 1 <= |a|
        invariant forall k :: 0 <= k < |a| && a[k] == key ==> low <= k <= high
        decreases high - low + 1
    {
        var mid := (low + high) / 2;
        if a[mid] < key {
            low := mid + 1;
        } else if a[mid] > key {
            high := mid - 1;
        } else {
            index := mid;
            return;
        }
    }
}
```

This code:
- Uses a `while` loop instead of recursion.
- Has proper preconditions (sorted array) and postconditions (correct index or -1).
- Includes loop invariants to help Dafny verify correctness.
- Handles empty sequences (the loop won’t execute, returns -1).
- Is efficient with O(log n) time complexity.
