Looking at the previous attempt, the loop invariants are not being maintained because when we update `left` or `right`, we need to prove that the new values still satisfy the invariants. The key issue is that the invariants about excluded pairs need to be maintained when we move the pointers.

Here's the corrected solution:

```dafny
method TwoSum(a: array<int>, target: int) returns (i: int, j: int)
  requires a.Length >= 2
  requires forall k :: 0 <= k < a.Length - 1 ==> a[k] <= a[k+1]
  requires exists i0, j0 :: 0 <= i0 < a.Length && 0 <= j0 < a.Length && i0 != j0 && a[i0] + a[j0] == target
  ensures 0 <= i < a.Length && 0 <= j < a.Length && i != j
  ensures a[i] + a[j] == target
{
  var left := 0;
  var right := a.Length - 1;
  
  while left < right
    invariant 0 <= left < a.Length
    invariant 0 <= right < a.Length
    invariant left < right
    invariant forall k :: 0 <= k < left ==> forall l :: left <= l < a.Length ==> a[k] + a[l] != target
    invariant forall k :: 0 <= k <= right ==> forall l :: right < l < a.Length ==> a[k] + a[l] != target
    decreases right - left
  {
    var sum := a[left] + a[right];
    if sum == target {
      i := left;
      j := right;
      return;
    } else if sum < target {
      // When sum < target, since array is sorted, a[left] is too small
      // So we can safely move left forward
      left := left + 1;
    } else {
      // When sum > target, since array is sorted, a[right] is too large
      // So we can safely move right backward
      right := right - 1;
    }
  }
  
  // Since precondition guarantees existence, we will never reach here
  i := -1;
  j := -1;
}
```

The key changes made:
1. Simplified the invariant structure to use nested `forall` quantifiers which are easier for Dafny to verify
2. The invariants now properly state that for any element before `left`, when paired with any element from `left` onwards, the sum is not the target
3. Similarly, for any element up to `right`, when paired with any element after `right`, the sum is not the target
4. The sorted array property ensures that when we move `left` forward (because sum < target), the new `left` position still satisfies the invariants, and similarly when we move `right` backward

This solution maintains the two-pointer approach and should verify correctly with Dafny.
