We need to rewrite the recursive `CountCharacters` method into an iterative one.  
The typical recursive version counts characters in a string by processing one character and then recursing on the rest.  
The iterative version will use a loop to traverse the string.

Here’s the plan:

- Use a `while` loop with an index variable.
- Maintain an invariant that the count so far equals the number of characters processed.
- The loop runs from `0` to `|s|`.

Edge cases:
- Empty string: loop doesn’t execute, returns 0.
- Non-empty string: loop processes each character.

Here’s the Dafny code:

```dafny
method CountCharacters(s: string) returns (count: int)
    ensures count == |s|
{
    count := 0;
    var i := 0;
    while i < |s|
        invariant 0 <= i <= |s|
        invariant count == i
    {
        count := count + 1;
        i := i + 1;
    }
}
```
